			"Message": "style(Common): Normalize tables, comments, and list indent\n\nConsistent formatting across Architecture.md, README.md, and Source/IPC/Channel.rs: align table pipes, soft-wrap long blockquote lines, convert em dashes to hyphens in non-prose contexts, fix list-item indentation, and normalize comment whitespace in the legacy channels block.\n\nThe README CHANGELOG bullet now uses the same indent depth as every other sub-item, the Shim Compatibility table renders uniformly in markdown renderers, and the legacy wire-shape doc block in Channel.rs follows the same paragraph style as the rest of the file.",
			"SHA": "9c99fb9f965e05f60b1e5e35ad1f6e020e241ee5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T22:34:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				365,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Common): Add Shim Compatibility section to Architecture documentation\n\nDocument the Land deep-shim interception system in the crate's Architecture.md, covering both the 🟠 Low-Level Shim (TierShim=Own|Preempt, JavaScript prototype hooks) and the 🔵 Coverage Shim (TierShim=Proxy|Replace, service-level routing and audit logging) with a comparison table and gating details.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Insert a new Shim Compatibility section between the Common/ directory tree diagram and the Project Maintainers footer\n- Add a two-column comparison table distinguishing the shim tiers by purpose, mechanism, and env var gate (TierShim, default None — zero overhead)\n- Note that no shim-specific modules live in Common; shim events route through Wind/Mountain/Cocoon\n- Reference the external Shim documentation at /doc/low-level-shim\n\nImpact: Architecture document now accurately reflects the dual-tier interception architecture, making it discoverable for contributors working on shim integration across Element crates.",
			"SHA": "c8deee027b61710c410941d13506237149b4a2f8"
